  "body": {
    "id": "thm:blind-iff",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Under the hypotheses of the blind ratio expansion, define\n\\[\n d_{nm}=\\sqrt{\\frac n{\\mu r}}\\left[1\\wedge\n \\frac B{\\lambda_{nm}}\\left\\{\n q^{-1}\\sqrt{(n\\vee m)\\log(e(n+m))}+q^{-3}\\log(en)\n \\right\\}\\right].\n\\]\nThen\n\\[\n \\left|\\mathcal L(\\widehat U^{\\mathrm B},U)-\\rho_{nm}\\right|=O_P(d_{nm}),\n \\qquad\n |\\widehat\\rho_{nm}-\\rho_{nm}|=O_P(d_{nm}).\n\\]\nConsequently, in every subregime where the explicit comparison \\(d_{nm}=O(b_{nm})\\) holds,\n\\[\n \\mathcal L(\\widehat U^{\\mathrm B},U)=O_P(b_{nm})\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n \\rho_{nm}=O_P(b_{nm})\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n \\widehat\\rho_{nm}=O_P(b_{nm}).\n\\]\nIn that subregime, \\(\\widehat\\rho_{nm}/b_{nm}\\to\\infty\\) implies failure of the frontier rate.  Without \\(d_{nm}=O(b_{nm})\\), the observed discrepancy is certified only up to the explicit \\(d_{nm}\\) resolution.",
